1
00:00:05,405 --> 00:00:09,242
It's the Seika era,
in the democratic country of Nipponia.

2
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:13,113
A huge ruling party has held power
for a long time.

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,951
This once-rich country is now
on the edge of a cliff.

4
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:20,220
The gap between rich and poor
keeps growing.

5
00:00:20,286 --> 00:00:22,422
Both blue-collar workers
and yakuza have no money.

6
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:29,963
In Nagatanicho, the center of this nation,
a great thief has landed.

7
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,465
Her surname is Kisaragi,
her given name is Yayoi.

8
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:34,067
Weren't you an election consultant?

9
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:36,936
I quit that and became Miyabi's secretary.

10
00:00:37,003 --> 00:00:38,972
I'm glad we had a fair fight.

11
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,274
We should thank the great thief.

12
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:43,510
A tanuki sniffing out the scent of money,

13
00:00:43,576 --> 00:00:45,645
and a tanuki sniffing out shadiness.

14
00:00:46,946 --> 00:00:49,649
The gong for this battle of deception
is about to ring!

15
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:52,318
PoliticaLupin!

16
00:00:55,755 --> 00:00:58,992
SECOND KAZAMATSURI CABINET
SET TO START

17
00:01:26,052 --> 00:01:29,389
Hey, you lounging there.
How did you get in?

18
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:31,491
Doors of multi-purpose buildings
take me only a minute.

19
00:01:31,558 --> 00:01:33,660
You should replace it
with the latest lock.

20
00:01:33,726 --> 00:01:35,829
I shouldn't have lent a thief my room.

21
00:01:35,895 --> 00:01:39,566
I'm a great thief. Besides, the room
you lent me can't really be called a room.

22
00:01:39,632 --> 00:01:43,269
It's a storage closet.
No windows, bad airflow. It's the worst.

23
00:01:43,336 --> 00:01:44,437
If you hate it, get out.

24
00:01:44,504 --> 00:01:46,706
This place is close to Nagatanicho.

25
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:50,176
Do you not enjoy seeing a cute girl
every day?

26
00:01:50,743 --> 00:01:53,646
Hey, if you dare lay a hand on me,
I'll kill you.

27
00:01:55,281 --> 00:01:56,616
Shut up, you squirt.

28
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,018
Yes?

29
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:01,087
Good morning, Mr. Kiuchi.

30
00:02:01,154 --> 00:02:03,123
Oh, good morning.

31
00:02:04,891 --> 00:02:06,059
Wait, just a second.

32
00:02:12,499 --> 00:02:13,967
I have a favor to ask.

33
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:16,970
What is it? Should I tell Mr. Shiro?

34
00:02:17,036 --> 00:02:18,138
No, it's a secret.

35
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:24,511
Mr. Kiuchi.

36
00:02:29,749 --> 00:02:30,817
Mr. Kiuchi.

37
00:02:31,384 --> 00:02:34,487
After using the "seasonal greetings"
to pay for our expenses,

38
00:02:34,554 --> 00:02:37,557
this is the share split between me,
Rui, and you, Inui.

39
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:39,626
Isn't this a bit lacking?
There was more, right?

40
00:02:39,692 --> 00:02:41,794
I made a political donation
to Mr. Hachimaki.

41
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:43,062
You mean that Hachimaki?

42
00:02:43,129 --> 00:02:45,965
He had to borrow money, and his deposit
of three million was confiscated.

43
00:02:46,032 --> 00:02:47,901
So I asked Rui to donate to him.

44
00:02:47,967 --> 00:02:49,035
With stolen money?

45
00:02:49,102 --> 00:02:50,737
Money itself is blameless, you know.

46
00:02:50,803 --> 00:02:52,205
What a waste.

47
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:56,209
I give half of the money I steal
to people who don't have any.

48
00:02:56,276 --> 00:02:58,378
That's my policy, and I won't budge on it.

49
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:01,681
No matter how clean a pond is,

50
00:03:01,748 --> 00:03:03,883
if you don't change the water
and let it flow,

51
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:07,320
it stagnates, turns muddy, and rots.

52
00:03:07,921 --> 00:03:10,857
The Cabinet rarely ever sees change, huh.

53
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:14,427
Everything in Nagatanicho
remains unchanged with near certainty.

54
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:16,930
Because it never sees change, it's solid.

55
00:03:16,996 --> 00:03:20,900
That's why the real economic growth rate
has stayed flat for 30 years.

56
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:25,238
Aren't you going to change that,
Mr. Natsume?

57
00:03:25,305 --> 00:03:28,141
Oh. We need to talk
about the stolen election funds.

58
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:30,310
This is Mr. Kiuchi's schedule of that day.

59
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:36,449
Mr. Kiuchi said one of the secretaries
was the culprit.

60
00:03:39,953 --> 00:03:42,455
He left the bag containing the cash
right on the desk,

61
00:03:43,022 --> 00:03:45,992
and had left his seat a few times
during that day.

62
00:03:50,029 --> 00:03:53,132
They are all paralyzed by suspicion
and quite nervous now.

63
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:57,537
Did Mr. Shiro tell you to investigate?

64
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,607
If they find out I'm suspecting them,

65
00:04:00,673 --> 00:04:02,875
nobody is going to feel good about it.

66
00:04:03,509 --> 00:04:05,979
We can't just ask the Cabinet Intelligence
to look into it.

67
00:04:06,045 --> 00:04:06,980
I'm honored, but…

68
00:04:07,046 --> 00:04:10,683
Natsume, I chose you because
you know our secretaries so well.

69
00:04:12,485 --> 00:04:16,856
What a troublesome business.
We aren't detectives!

70
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:18,725
And that's not the only thing.

71
00:04:18,791 --> 00:04:19,926
Huh?

72
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:23,263
The election funding issue
has nothing to do with me.

73
00:04:23,329 --> 00:04:25,965
But isn't Chiba 17
the district you were in charge of?

74
00:04:26,032 --> 00:04:29,269
With all due respect,
I was just helping out…

75
00:04:29,335 --> 00:04:33,773
The Financial Director
is involved in all money matters.

76
00:04:35,174 --> 00:04:36,142
And besides…

77
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:37,543
There's more?

78
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,746
Secretary-General Kazamatsuri
is also suspicious,

79
00:04:39,812 --> 00:04:43,316
and Mr. Shiro is defending
his own secretary.

80
00:04:44,984 --> 00:04:46,686
Why don't you go probe around a bit?

81
00:04:47,987 --> 00:04:50,390
I made an effort to avoid
getting close to anyone,

82
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:53,026
and to maintain a proper distance,

83
00:04:53,092 --> 00:04:55,028
and the result of all of that

84
00:04:55,094 --> 00:04:57,530
is that all three of them

85
00:04:57,597 --> 00:05:01,868
think of me as their personal servant.

86
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:06,773
Jeez…

87
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:10,209
Don't give me more work.

88
00:05:10,276 --> 00:05:13,513
Who the hell stole that money?!

89
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:17,850
How to get close to the safe
in the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office…

90
00:05:18,551 --> 00:05:21,688
The current Chief Cabinet Secretary
is Shokichi Takekoshi,

91
00:05:21,754 --> 00:05:23,189
the brother-in-law of Shiro Kobayakawa.

92
00:05:23,256 --> 00:05:25,692
Miyabi has hardly ever spoken to him.

93
00:05:26,693 --> 00:05:29,796
If we could get inside the Secretary's
office we'd know what the layout is.

94
00:05:29,862 --> 00:05:32,965
If only Miyabi
had been a member of the Kokuji party…

95
00:05:33,032 --> 00:05:36,336
If she held a position in the ruling party
she could help us get close.

96
00:05:36,402 --> 00:05:39,138
I think so too.

97
00:05:39,706 --> 00:05:41,674
Join the Kokuji party.

98
00:05:41,741 --> 00:05:43,176
If you join the Kokuji party,

99
00:05:43,242 --> 00:05:45,845
you get ten million yen
from party subsidies.

100
00:05:45,912 --> 00:05:48,481
Even if you lose the next election,

101
00:05:48,548 --> 00:05:50,817
you get one million yen a month.

102
00:05:50,883 --> 00:05:52,452
Already thinking about the next election?

103
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:54,987
That's just the way politicians are.

104
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:59,325
If we lose,
the secretaries will be out of a job.

105
00:06:00,626 --> 00:06:02,662
We'll be dragging them down with us.

106
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:04,364
I'm not joining the Kokuji party.

107
00:06:05,798 --> 00:06:07,166
I'm not joining.

108
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,335
Talk her into it. You're good at that.

109
00:06:09,402 --> 00:06:10,937
I don't feel like it.

110
00:06:11,003 --> 00:06:13,906
I mean, that girl is dead serious.

111
00:06:16,242 --> 00:06:18,544
Miyabi is seriously

112
00:06:18,611 --> 00:06:20,847
and honestly trying to be a politician.

113
00:06:20,913 --> 00:06:22,248
You made her do that.

114
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:24,951
It feels like I'm deceiving her.

115
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:26,352
Because you are.

116
00:06:26,419 --> 00:06:29,455
If she had just a slightly
more casual attitude about it,

117
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:32,525
I could concentrate on my work
with zero guilt.

118
00:06:32,592 --> 00:06:34,861
What a selfish thing to say.

119
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:39,832
Anyway, I'll leave my main job aside
for a moment and work for Miyabi's sake.

120
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:41,968
I'll earn my paycheck. First is this.

121
00:06:42,034 --> 00:06:44,871
This account, Wasshi,
which slandered Miyabi a lot.

122
00:06:44,937 --> 00:06:47,006
Oh, I saw this account a lot
during the election.

123
00:06:49,976 --> 00:06:51,077
This post.

124
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:54,947
"Miyabi Kobayakawa
spent a lot of money on a host,

125
00:06:55,014 --> 00:06:57,350
got dumped, and got in a brawl outside.
Have some shame!"

126
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:59,552
Not even a tabloid
would write stuff like this!

127
00:06:59,619 --> 00:07:01,754
The one who gave that host money
was Miyabi's friend,

128
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:03,256
and she was fighting for her!

129
00:07:03,322 --> 00:07:06,926
We have proof, so I had a lawyer
file a disclosure request.

130
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:10,696
Next, there is this. A video on NowTube.

131
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:14,300
When I traced the source,
it was a job-posting site.

132
00:07:14,801 --> 00:07:17,570
The site itself is ordinary,

133
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:21,407
but multiple listings for creating
"Miyabi Kobayakawa" videos popped up.

134
00:07:21,474 --> 00:07:25,978
Who made them create
slanderous videos about Miyabi?

135
00:07:26,546 --> 00:07:27,647
And so,

136
00:07:28,247 --> 00:07:31,517
Rui applied for the video creation job
and got hired!

137
00:07:31,584 --> 00:07:32,618
Huh?

138
00:07:32,685 --> 00:07:34,720
DIET MEMBERS' OFFICE

139
00:07:39,225 --> 00:07:41,561
Hello, Miss Miyabi.

140
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:43,596
My name is Ginji.

141
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,298
Masakado's…

142
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:46,866
"Oi"?

143
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,702
Oi? Is that an English word?

144
00:07:49,769 --> 00:07:53,573
It means I'm Masakado's
older sister's son.

145
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,575
How do you say that in English?

146
00:07:56,542 --> 00:07:57,543
"Nephew."

147
00:07:58,478 --> 00:07:59,312
Nephew?

148
00:07:59,378 --> 00:08:00,546
Nephew.

149
00:08:02,215 --> 00:08:03,950
Come on in.

150
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:06,752
Which committee did you get assigned to?

151
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,988
The Environment Committee.

152
00:08:09,956 --> 00:08:12,291
Many independents get put
into that committee.

153
00:08:15,862 --> 00:08:16,696
Excuse me.

154
00:08:16,762 --> 00:08:19,799
Mr. Kiuchi, the secretary said
that you, Mr. Honma,

155
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:24,070
are a veteran with 40 years of experience
as a secretary, and I should rely on you.

156
00:08:24,136 --> 00:08:25,471
For what?

157
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:28,875
Neither I nor my secretaries
know anything.

158
00:08:28,941 --> 00:08:32,612
I figured if I belonged to a party,
there would be study sessions and such.

159
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:35,414
A computer and telephone
were provided for me,

160
00:08:35,481 --> 00:08:38,784
and since a vendor came by to pitch
a multifunction printer, I ordered one.

161
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:42,188
But what should I do from now on?

162
00:08:42,255 --> 00:08:43,422
Mr. Honma.

163
00:08:50,796 --> 00:08:52,498
Who are your secretaries?

164
00:08:52,565 --> 00:08:54,834
My chief public secretary

165
00:08:54,901 --> 00:08:56,168
is my friend Kaoru.

166
00:08:56,736 --> 00:08:59,005
She worked freelance as an interpreter.

167
00:08:59,572 --> 00:09:00,606
I see.

168
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:03,543
My second public secretary is Momoko.

169
00:09:03,609 --> 00:09:06,112
She used to run a popular diner.

170
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,216
I see!

171
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:13,185
In other words, a group of amateurs.

172
00:09:13,252 --> 00:09:16,589
Kaoru majored in political science,
and Momoko is quick with calculations.

173
00:09:19,258 --> 00:09:20,860
What about Yayoi Kisaragi?

174
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:23,896
She's my private secretary.
She didn't want to go public.

175
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:25,798
She didn't want to?

176
00:09:25,865 --> 00:09:28,501
Public secretaries are paid
with tax money, right?

177
00:09:29,135 --> 00:09:31,137
-Well, yes.
-I prefer private.

178
00:09:31,203 --> 00:09:33,306
Make me your private secretary.

179
00:09:33,372 --> 00:09:36,142
I'm fine with being paid half as much.
Consider me a part-time worker.

180
00:09:36,709 --> 00:09:39,145
I think her consulting work
is keeping her busy.

181
00:09:39,211 --> 00:09:41,514
She said she was taking a break
from consulting though.

182
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:42,848
Is that so?

183
00:09:45,551 --> 00:09:47,119
If you want to make policies,

184
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:49,922
have you found a policy secretary?

185
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:52,692
A policy secretary?

186
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:56,862
You can qualify by working as
a lawyer or certified public accountant,

187
00:09:56,929 --> 00:09:59,665
or by being a secretary for ten years,

188
00:09:59,732 --> 00:10:02,335
after receiving
the relevant certification.

189
00:10:02,401 --> 00:10:03,469
I've received it, too.

190
00:10:04,036 --> 00:10:05,571
Ten years as a secretary?

191
00:10:10,376 --> 00:10:12,845
If you join the Kokuji party,
I can introduce you to someone.

192
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:18,484
When you're in, you can learn everything
about being a secretary and a politician.

193
00:10:18,551 --> 00:10:20,019
Right, Mr. Honma?

194
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:21,420
Yes.

195
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:26,525
Were you told by my father to invite me?

196
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:34,367
Thank you for your time. Excuse me.

197
00:10:36,602 --> 00:10:37,870
-Nephew?
-Nephew.

198
00:10:40,706 --> 00:10:44,176
Your recruiting skills are terrible.

199
00:10:44,243 --> 00:10:47,747
I talked to her. I did the bare minimum.

200
00:10:48,347 --> 00:10:50,449
Is the bare minimum all you need to do?

201
00:10:50,516 --> 00:10:54,253
You better give it your all.
What the heck was that "nephew" stuff?

202
00:10:55,354 --> 00:10:57,490
I'm heading to the library.

203
00:10:59,025 --> 00:11:01,761
Such a nice place.
Maybe I should move in too.

204
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:02,662
There's a rooftop.

205
00:11:02,728 --> 00:11:04,063
-For a beer garden?
-Or BBQ!

206
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:05,331
The best parts of summer.

207
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:06,232
Don't you dare.

208
00:11:06,298 --> 00:11:07,600
-You mean, do it?
-Reverse psych?

209
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,969
I meant it.
You came to report, didn't you?

210
00:11:10,536 --> 00:11:12,605
How did that video-making gig turn out?

211
00:11:13,272 --> 00:11:14,540
Okay! Reporting!

212
00:11:15,274 --> 00:11:16,776
According to the job poster,

213
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:19,745
they don't need videos
of Miyabi Kobayakawa anymore.

214
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:23,549
Instead, they sent me a script asking
if I could make this kind of video.

215
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:26,085
So I followed the script

216
00:11:26,152 --> 00:11:29,021
and made a video.

217
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:29,955
This is it.

218
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:33,025
Speechless!
Foreigners are splurging welfare money!

219
00:11:33,092 --> 00:11:35,628
An extinction threat!
Nipponia is turning into a trash heap!

220
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,897
The taxes you paid…

221
00:11:37,963 --> 00:11:40,633
I ignored my own feelings
and worked on it.

222
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:43,903
It was done really quickly,
and the client liked it.

223
00:11:43,969 --> 00:11:45,671
And after some flattering,

224
00:11:45,738 --> 00:11:47,873
we talked directly on Descord.

225
00:11:48,441 --> 00:11:52,378
Why did you make videos
criticizing Miyabi?

226
00:11:52,445 --> 00:11:54,847
Political videos do well during elections.

227
00:11:54,914 --> 00:11:58,918
Miyabi videos were trending.
I might earn 400,000 yen next month.

228
00:11:58,984 --> 00:12:01,187
Amazing. Respect!

229
00:12:01,253 --> 00:12:02,088
Thanks.

230
00:12:02,154 --> 00:12:03,789
Dad, play with me!

231
00:12:03,856 --> 00:12:06,726
Quiet, Dad is working now.

232
00:12:09,028 --> 00:12:13,332
Anyway, the Miyabi videos
are so last season. We do this now.

233
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,934
"Foreigners are dangerous" videos.

234
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,672
Is the info in the script I got
really true?

235
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:21,507
It seems in reality,

236
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:24,977
foreign households only take up 3%
of welfare funds, not 33% like the script.

237
00:12:26,112 --> 00:12:27,880
I don't know and don't care.

238
00:12:28,447 --> 00:12:32,084
A complete lack of morals.
Well, a thief like me can't say much.

239
00:12:32,151 --> 00:12:36,388
Wait, their goal is just making money?

240
00:12:36,455 --> 00:12:38,724
-It seems so.
-It will be hard to stop those!

241
00:12:38,791 --> 00:12:41,160
Sometimes foreign forces do it too.

242
00:12:41,227 --> 00:12:43,662
Moneymaking and political agendas.

243
00:12:43,729 --> 00:12:48,000
With "phone farms,"
you can fake viewer counts.

244
00:12:48,067 --> 00:12:51,003
If you get a good amount of views in,
the video goes trending,

245
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:52,471
which gets it even more views.

246
00:12:52,538 --> 00:12:53,372
It never ends.

247
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:56,041
It's rage bait.

248
00:12:56,108 --> 00:12:59,278
Designed to make people react in anger.
Modern alchemy.

249
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:01,547
How did the disclosure request
against Wasshi go?

250
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,683
Wasshi's videos were from a company
called Ponz Next.

251
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:06,452
Their capital is ten million yen.

252
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:09,455
They are a web and ad company, it seems,

253
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:11,457
but there is no more info online.

254
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:13,859
Meaning someone is posting
while slacking off at work?

255
00:13:13,926 --> 00:13:14,860
Maybe?

256
00:13:14,927 --> 00:13:16,996
Employee or part-timer, who knows.

257
00:13:17,062 --> 00:13:18,330
Ponz Next…

258
00:13:19,231 --> 00:13:21,600
I remember it from
a political funding report.

259
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:23,102
POLITICAL FUNDING
RECEIPT DATABASE

260
00:13:23,169 --> 00:13:24,637
PONZ NEXT

261
00:13:26,238 --> 00:13:27,840
More results than I thought.

262
00:13:27,907 --> 00:13:30,442
The scent of money! Let's investigate.

263
00:13:30,509 --> 00:13:32,178
You guys can't handle this.

264
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,081
This is my specialty.

265
00:13:44,857 --> 00:13:46,325
-Momo.
-Yes?

266
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:50,563
Just how busy is Yayoi
with her consulting work?

267
00:13:50,629 --> 00:13:53,766
Huh? I think she isn't busy at all.

268
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,569
She used to be a regular at my shop.

269
00:13:56,635 --> 00:13:59,505
She doesn't have that much money either.

270
00:14:00,906 --> 00:14:03,342
I'll go search for cheap Chiba properties.

271
00:14:03,409 --> 00:14:05,711
Somewhere convenient,
easy for people to visit.

272
00:14:05,778 --> 00:14:08,047
Cheapness comes first, then convenience.

273
00:14:08,113 --> 00:14:09,448
I'm off.

274
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:11,016
-Take care.
-Take care.

275
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,486
Hey, we received this.

276
00:14:14,553 --> 00:14:18,324
"The Women Lawmakers' League
for Promoting Women in Politics."

277
00:14:18,390 --> 00:14:21,760
Hosted by Misaki Utsunomiya
of the Minyu Party.

278
00:14:21,827 --> 00:14:25,998
Multi-party. Even independents can join.
Shall we check it out?

279
00:14:26,732 --> 00:14:31,437
The women's restroom on the second floor
of the Lower House

280
00:14:31,503 --> 00:14:35,040
has only a quarter as many stalls
as the men's.

281
00:14:35,107 --> 00:14:38,344
As you may know, it always has long lines.

282
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:41,981
We'll have more and more
female Diet members.

283
00:14:42,047 --> 00:14:45,751
If we don't start renovation now,
it will be too late.

284
00:14:46,418 --> 00:14:48,921
We will strongly demand this.

285
00:14:48,988 --> 00:14:53,192
If we don't speak up, nothing changes.

286
00:14:53,792 --> 00:14:54,793
Thank you for today.

287
00:14:56,028 --> 00:14:57,329
Welcome.

288
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:59,164
I'm the host, Utsunomiya.

289
00:15:00,132 --> 00:15:01,767
-I'm Miyabi…
-Kobayakawa.

290
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:05,137
I watched your election.
It was exhilarating.

291
00:15:05,204 --> 00:15:06,238
Thanks.

292
00:15:07,606 --> 00:15:11,243
Are you okay?
You must feel really lost right now.

293
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,012
I'm completely lost.

294
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:13,946
Yeah.

295
00:15:14,013 --> 00:15:15,047
-Ms. Matsushita.
-Yes.

296
00:15:15,614 --> 00:15:18,083
She is my secretary.
Ask her anything you don't know.

297
00:15:19,285 --> 00:15:21,186
-Thank you.
-Pleased to meet you.

298
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:25,658
I'm sure you already know,
but politics is an old-men's paradise.

299
00:15:25,724 --> 00:15:26,458
Yes.

300
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,896
If women connect and make work easier,

301
00:15:30,963 --> 00:15:32,431
more women will be elected.

302
00:15:32,498 --> 00:15:36,802
Then we can push policies
in untouched areas.

303
00:15:36,869 --> 00:15:39,471
This is the kind of forward-thinking
our league upholds.

304
00:15:39,538 --> 00:15:41,473
Please let me join.

305
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,309
You're very welcome.

306
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:46,745
I belong to about ten other leagues.

307
00:15:46,812 --> 00:15:49,214
There are many cross-party members,
so if you're interested…

308
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:50,649
I am!

309
00:15:53,319 --> 00:15:56,188
Don't rush. Look closely, then decide.

310
00:15:56,255 --> 00:15:58,357
Each has costs and dues.

311
00:15:59,825 --> 00:16:02,027
Sometimes you pay out of pocket.

312
00:16:02,094 --> 00:16:03,028
I see.

313
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:06,899
KOKUJI PARTY

314
00:16:07,599 --> 00:16:09,468
What is your business?

315
00:16:09,535 --> 00:16:11,203
SADAHARU IENAGA

316
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:13,906
It isn't really urgent, but…

317
00:16:17,009 --> 00:16:18,711
I heard you objected

318
00:16:18,777 --> 00:16:22,614
to the election budget allocation

319
00:16:22,681 --> 00:16:25,851
that the Secretary General and I made.

320
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:29,455
What is your reason?

321
00:16:29,521 --> 00:16:30,622
I…

322
00:16:30,689 --> 00:16:34,526
In the House election,
the Kokuji Party didn't gain seats.

323
00:16:35,027 --> 00:16:38,630
We lost seats. Do you feel responsible?

324
00:16:39,732 --> 00:16:41,900
I was appointed Finance Director…

325
00:16:43,235 --> 00:16:44,436
So…

326
00:16:47,272 --> 00:16:48,707
My main duty

327
00:16:49,208 --> 00:16:52,511
is simply handling party accounts.

328
00:16:52,578 --> 00:16:54,747
Handling party accounts?

329
00:16:57,082 --> 00:16:59,718
Your job is to stamp.

330
00:17:00,285 --> 00:17:02,154
Just stamp the documents.

331
00:17:02,221 --> 00:17:06,325
Stamp the documents we tell you to stamp.

332
00:17:06,892 --> 00:17:09,995
That's your job as Finance Director.

333
00:17:10,829 --> 00:17:11,663
Understand?

334
00:17:13,465 --> 00:17:15,034
Do you understand?

335
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,035
Yes.

336
00:17:23,242 --> 00:17:24,743
May I join you?

337
00:17:27,579 --> 00:17:28,447
Go ahead.

338
00:17:34,119 --> 00:17:35,421
No appetite?

339
00:17:36,188 --> 00:17:37,189
Not really.

340
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:43,228
Eel is going extinct,
yet it's on the menu, huh.

341
00:17:43,295 --> 00:17:44,496
Let's eat.

342
00:17:49,768 --> 00:17:51,770
You eat it knowing that?

343
00:17:52,337 --> 00:17:54,440
Don't you feel doubt?

344
00:17:54,506 --> 00:17:58,744
If it's sold, I eat it.
Like if there's money, I take it.

345
00:17:58,811 --> 00:18:02,915
If you can make money writing lies online,
you would do it, right?

346
00:18:02,981 --> 00:18:03,849
Would you do it?

347
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:04,750
You wouldn't?

348
00:18:04,817 --> 00:18:05,784
I wouldn't.

349
00:18:05,851 --> 00:18:09,721
Even if most wouldn't, some will.
Humans are evil creatures.

350
00:18:09,788 --> 00:18:11,690
You believe in original sin?

351
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:14,093
I prefer believing people are good.

352
00:18:14,159 --> 00:18:16,829
Me too. But the world isn't like that.

353
00:18:16,895 --> 00:18:19,465
You must design systems
so it's hard to do evil,

354
00:18:19,531 --> 00:18:21,133
or it fills with evil people.

355
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,634
For now, eel is being sold,

356
00:18:22,701 --> 00:18:25,304
so the world
is full of eel-eating evil people.

357
00:18:26,305 --> 00:18:28,740
When I eat eel,

358
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:32,344
I eat with the intent
to drive eels extinct.

359
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,583
Research on farmed eel is progressing.

360
00:18:37,649 --> 00:18:42,254
The Fisheries Agency put 700 million yen
in last year's supplementary budget

361
00:18:42,321 --> 00:18:45,157
into artificial eel research and rollout.

362
00:18:45,224 --> 00:18:46,959
Artificial eels will be on tables soon.

363
00:18:47,025 --> 00:18:48,994
Wonderful story.
Bad people will disappear.

364
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:52,831
Saving eel from extinction
is also a politician's job.

365
00:18:54,833 --> 00:18:57,736
Can politics solve Internet fake news?

366
00:19:01,406 --> 00:19:03,308
It's dangerous for those in power

367
00:19:04,109 --> 00:19:06,812
to get to decide what is "fake news".

368
00:19:06,879 --> 00:19:08,814
Nipponia has freedom of expression.

369
00:19:08,881 --> 00:19:10,349
Really.

370
00:19:11,283 --> 00:19:12,918
Personally,

371
00:19:13,752 --> 00:19:18,390
I think we could demonetize
videos related to politics,

372
00:19:18,457 --> 00:19:20,159
at least during elections.

373
00:19:20,225 --> 00:19:21,693
That's very helpful.

374
00:19:22,694 --> 00:19:28,467
I'm thinking of asking a company
to handle slander against Miyabi.

375
00:19:28,534 --> 00:19:29,635
Maybe you need it.

376
00:19:30,202 --> 00:19:32,471
Would this company be good?
Do you know it?

377
00:19:38,977 --> 00:19:41,246
PONZ NEXT

378
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:54,393
Many Diet members
seem to use this company.

379
00:19:55,627 --> 00:19:58,664
I don't recommend it.

380
00:19:58,730 --> 00:20:00,132
Huh? Why?

381
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,935
I think they only accept jobs
from Kokuji Party members.

382
00:20:06,238 --> 00:20:10,576
Do you know this account
that slandered Miyabi?

383
00:20:12,344 --> 00:20:14,112
WASSHI

384
00:20:14,179 --> 00:20:16,448
Looking back,

385
00:20:16,515 --> 00:20:18,517
it's not just Miyabi.

386
00:20:18,584 --> 00:20:21,253
Many opposition members are slandered too.

387
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:23,322
In many cases, it borders on defamation.

388
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:26,091
If that's all, then this would just be
a common malicious account.

389
00:20:26,158 --> 00:20:28,026
But I noticed something big.

390
00:20:28,527 --> 00:20:31,230
It's active on weekdays from nine to six,

391
00:20:31,296 --> 00:20:32,764
and off on weekends and holidays.

392
00:20:32,831 --> 00:20:34,099
Like a salaryman.

393
00:20:34,166 --> 00:20:36,235
Ponz Next is doing it as a job.

394
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:39,838
The one ordering it is the Kokuji Party.

395
00:20:41,873 --> 00:20:44,476
The president of Ponz Next
is Uchiteru Tomino.

396
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:47,045
This guy himself isn't a big deal.

397
00:20:47,813 --> 00:20:50,549
His relative is a big shot.

398
00:20:52,317 --> 00:20:55,821
The executive secretary
of the Kokuji Party, Sadaharu Ienaga.

399
00:20:55,887 --> 00:20:57,089
-A politician?
-No.

400
00:20:57,155 --> 00:20:59,825
Not Ienaga.
This guy is a Kokuji Party staff member.

401
00:21:00,392 --> 00:21:03,662
He climbed the ranks and has been
the treasurer for over 50 years.

402
00:21:03,729 --> 00:21:06,598
Thanks to that, even cabinet ministers
can't talk back to him.

403
00:21:06,665 --> 00:21:08,133
Isn't Natsume the treasurer?

404
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,169
The Finance Director is just a title.
The real power rests with Ienaga.

405
00:21:11,236 --> 00:21:13,038
What the heck? What?

406
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:15,073
This, this, and this too.

407
00:21:16,642 --> 00:21:18,910
These are companies with ties to Ienaga,

408
00:21:18,977 --> 00:21:21,246
taking on work from the Kokuji Party.

409
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:25,050
There's a rumor that this research company

410
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,786
took a job for 50 million yen
and got a 20 million yen kickback.

411
00:21:27,853 --> 00:21:31,590
What a dark treasure.
Is Ponz Next doing that too?

412
00:21:31,657 --> 00:21:32,858
Probably.

413
00:21:33,425 --> 00:21:35,961
My request for disclosure got accepted.

414
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:42,000
Ponz Next was behind this Wasshi account.

415
00:21:42,501 --> 00:21:44,603
They pretended to be civilians

416
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:49,308
to spread bad rumors
about your opposition and rivals.

417
00:21:50,075 --> 00:21:52,844
Where is the money coming from?
It's tax money, right?

418
00:21:52,911 --> 00:21:54,279
With all respect,

419
00:21:54,346 --> 00:21:57,616
even if some members have deals with them,

420
00:21:57,683 --> 00:22:00,385
we can't say the slander
is the Kokuji Party's request.

421
00:22:02,187 --> 00:22:06,325
I don't want a lawsuit.
It's troublesome, you know.

422
00:22:07,059 --> 00:22:11,330
If you could at least
delete the rumors about Miyabi,

423
00:22:11,897 --> 00:22:15,600
I could stay a see-no-evil,
hear-no-evil monkey.

424
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:23,408
I'm actually pretty angry.

425
00:22:26,578 --> 00:22:28,580
Hello. Everyone working hard?

426
00:22:28,647 --> 00:22:30,148
-Yes!
-I got food.

427
00:22:30,215 --> 00:22:31,983
Yay!

428
00:22:32,050 --> 00:22:33,418
I'll call Miyabi.

429
00:22:36,321 --> 00:22:38,156
Did you find a Chiba office?

430
00:22:38,223 --> 00:22:39,691
It's hard.

431
00:22:39,758 --> 00:22:42,461
Even though she's a Kobayakawa daughter,

432
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,996
they won't rent to someone
who beat a Kokuji Party member.

433
00:22:45,063 --> 00:22:47,399
All the landlords are Kokuji Party people.

434
00:22:47,466 --> 00:22:49,701
All of them… It's a wonder we won.

435
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:52,204
By 210 votes. A miracle!

436
00:22:52,270 --> 00:22:53,805
Yayoi.

437
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:55,240
How did your consulting go?

438
00:22:55,307 --> 00:22:56,241
It went fine today.

439
00:22:58,143 --> 00:23:00,178
What is everyone doing now?

440
00:23:02,447 --> 00:23:05,617
We're making a league for election reform.

441
00:23:05,684 --> 00:23:08,019
-Wow!
-Yes!

442
00:23:08,086 --> 00:23:09,721
-A league?
-Of Diet members.

443
00:23:09,788 --> 00:23:10,856
Here.

444
00:23:12,924 --> 00:23:16,395
To submit a bill in the Lower House,
we need 20 members.

445
00:23:16,461 --> 00:23:19,431
So it all starts
with gathering supporters.

446
00:23:19,498 --> 00:23:22,734
Now we're preparing materials
for the first meeting.

447
00:23:23,802 --> 00:23:24,770
I'll help.

448
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:35,680
Do you know Ponz Next?

449
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:38,316
Yes, it's related to Mr. Ienaga, right?

450
00:23:38,383 --> 00:23:39,251
Exactly.

451
00:23:39,317 --> 00:23:41,820
That company not only does PR,

452
00:23:41,887 --> 00:23:44,990
but also operates accounts
that spread slander.

453
00:23:45,056 --> 00:23:46,124
No way.

454
00:23:46,191 --> 00:23:48,693
Hard to believe, but I looked into it…

455
00:23:52,497 --> 00:23:54,466
It received more than 25 million yen

456
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:56,334
from the Kokuji Party Tokyo chapter,

457
00:23:56,401 --> 00:23:58,336
aside from donations
by other Diet members.

458
00:23:58,403 --> 00:24:01,006
We can't say
they aren't affiliated with us.

459
00:24:01,072 --> 00:24:05,277
This is terrible! I can't believe
they chose this sloppy method.

460
00:24:09,414 --> 00:24:13,452
What happens if I make this public?

461
00:24:14,686 --> 00:24:15,787
You would be cut off.

462
00:24:16,555 --> 00:24:18,957
Right?!

463
00:24:24,896 --> 00:24:27,566
I want to get angry, but I can't…

464
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:32,471
Maybe we should cut off Natsume?

465
00:24:33,538 --> 00:24:34,673
Your son

466
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:38,710
refused his own party's
support speech, didn't he?

467
00:24:38,777 --> 00:24:42,981
Maybe Mr. Natsume
has been a bad influence.

468
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:45,083
Otherwise,

469
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:48,019
there's no reason
we would have lost Chiba 17.

470
00:24:50,689 --> 00:24:52,858
We even used real money.

471
00:24:53,692 --> 00:24:56,528
There was some trouble there…

472
00:24:56,595 --> 00:24:59,030
Our boy is hard to handle.

473
00:24:59,097 --> 00:25:02,000
I raised him too gently.

474
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,403
Natsume is capable.

475
00:25:05,470 --> 00:25:06,905
Colorless.

476
00:25:07,706 --> 00:25:09,608
Not tied to any faction.
I like that about him.

477
00:25:10,775 --> 00:25:14,779
Please go easy on him.

478
00:25:16,448 --> 00:25:19,217
If you say so…

479
00:25:19,284 --> 00:25:20,252
Yes.

480
00:25:28,426 --> 00:25:30,795
-Here.
-I'll go to the House of Councillors.

481
00:25:30,862 --> 00:25:32,264
-Okay.
-Here.

482
00:25:32,330 --> 00:25:33,965
Then I'll go
to the House of Representatives.

483
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:34,966
I'm going too.

484
00:25:49,948 --> 00:25:51,483
ELECTION REFORM LEAGUE

485
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,952
After we've gathered people
for the league, what next?

486
00:25:56,288 --> 00:26:00,258
Consult the House research office,
hear from experts,

487
00:26:00,325 --> 00:26:03,762
deepen discussion, and firm up the bill.

488
00:26:03,828 --> 00:26:06,998
Also have National Diet Library staff

489
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:11,236
look into foreign precedents
and past data.

490
00:26:11,303 --> 00:26:13,204
Okay. Mic is ready.

491
00:26:14,139 --> 00:26:16,141
Did you find a policy secretary?

492
00:26:16,207 --> 00:26:18,009
We're recruiting on social media.

493
00:26:18,076 --> 00:26:20,045
I hope you find someone good.

494
00:26:20,111 --> 00:26:22,314
Oh, it's almost time.

495
00:26:31,623 --> 00:26:33,124
I'll take a look.

496
00:26:47,505 --> 00:26:50,208
Sorry for being late.

497
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:52,510
Oh, it's okay.

498
00:27:00,352 --> 00:27:03,221
Will it be hard as an independent?

499
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:04,623
Well…

500
00:27:04,689 --> 00:27:08,126
It's easier with horizontal connections.

501
00:27:09,094 --> 00:27:12,964
In your case, gathering 20 people
might take five years.

502
00:27:13,031 --> 00:27:13,965
Five years?

503
00:27:14,032 --> 00:27:16,468
A league about rethinking
hereditary politics

504
00:27:16,534 --> 00:27:19,871
won't do well with Kokuji members,
many of whom come from political families.

505
00:27:19,938 --> 00:27:23,208
Opposition members see you
as Shiro Kobayakawa's daughter

506
00:27:23,274 --> 00:27:24,476
and keep away.

507
00:27:24,542 --> 00:27:28,980
You must show each person
who you are to gain their understanding,

508
00:27:29,047 --> 00:27:32,484
earn their trust, and gather 20 people.

509
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:36,521
Then five more years of discussion.

510
00:27:36,588 --> 00:27:38,623
Ten years total.

511
00:27:38,690 --> 00:27:40,425
That's pretty standard.

512
